    <statement><p>Use difference quotients with <m>\Delta x = 0.1</m> and
<m>\Delta y = 0.1</m> to estimate <m>f_x(1,2)</m> and
<m>f_y(1,2)</m> where
<me>f(x,y) = e^{-x}\sin\mathopen{}\left(y\right).</me></p>
<p><m>f_x(1,2) \approx</m> <fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>f_y(1,2) \approx</m> <fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>Then give better estimates by using <m>\Delta x = 0.01</m> and
<m>\Delta y = 0.01</m>.</p>
<p><m>f_x(1,2) \approx</m> <fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p><m>f_y(1,2) \approx</m> <fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-0.31833</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-0.169548</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-0.332845</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-0.154762</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\Delta x=0.1</m> and <m>\Delta y =0.1</m>, we have the estimates:
<me>f_x(1,2) \approx \frac{f(1.1,2) - f(1,2)}{0.1}
         = \frac{e^{-1.1}\,\sin(2) - e^{-1}\,\sin(2)}{0.1}
         \approx \frac{0.302679 - 0.334512}{0.1} = -0.31833.</me>
and
<me>f_y(1,2) \approx \frac{f(1,2.1) - f(1,2)}{0.1}
	= \frac{e^{-1}\,\sin(2.1) - e^{-1}\,\sin(2)}{0.1}
        \approx \frac{0.317557 - 0.334512}{0.1} = -0.169548.</me>
Now, using <m>\Delta x=0.01</m> and <m>\Delta y=0.01</m>, we have the estimates:
<me>f_x(1,2) \approx \frac{f(1.01,2) - f(1,2)}{0.01}
        = \frac{e^{-1.01}\,\sin(2) - e^{-1}\,\sin(2)}{0.01}
        \approx \frac{0.331183 - 0.334512}{0.01} = -0.332845</me>
and
<me>f_x(1,2) \approx \frac{f(1,2.01) - f(1,2)}{0.01}
        = \frac{e^{-1}\,\sin(2.01) - e^{-1}\,\sin(2)}{0.01}
        \approx \frac{0.332964 - 0.334512}{0.01} = -0.154762.</me>



</solution>
